# Screens must stay thin

Files in `src/app/**` are expo-router routes. They should only compose other
pieces — not own logic.

## Do

- Import a `useX()` hook from `src/hooks/` for every non-trivial state machine.
- Import feature components from `src/components/<feature>/`.
- Pull types, constants, and API calls from `src/lib/<feature>/`.
- Keep the default export shape: the screen's component name can change, but
  the file path must stay (it defines the route).

## Don't

- No inline `fetch` / `axios` calls — move to `src/lib/<feature>/api.ts`.
- No inline `useState` chains longer than ~5 hooks — extract to
  `src/hooks/use-<feature>.ts`.
- No sub-component declarations over ~20 lines in the same file — move to
  `src/components/<feature>/`.
- Do not rename, move, or delete files under `src/app/` without knowing the
  route impact.

## Example

Good thin screen (reference):
[src/app/(tabs)/schedule.tsx](src/app/(tabs)/schedule.tsx) — 95 lines,
delegates to `useScheduleReminders()` and three feature components.
